  "reason": "The records collectively make the later strategy plausibly reconstructible. R2, R4, R5, R11, R15, and R18 establish high-energy or mechanical milling of elemental HEA powders followed by SPS, including the dependence of refinement and hardness on milling duration. R6 and R15 connect this route to grain refinement, solid-solution strengthening, and Hall–Petch strengthening, while R8 independently demonstrates nanocrystalline grain-boundary strengthening and R19 supplies closely related CoCrFe-based evidence for fine-grain and dislocation strengthening. SPS-driven densification, rapid diffusion, and phase retention are also supported by R3, R9, and R13. The exact CoCrFeNiTi composition, short 1–6 h milling window, 900–1000 °C SPS schedule, 83% FCC/17% BCC ratio, and Ti-specific phase-stabilization explanation are not directly disclosed, but an expert could plausibly combine the prior processing and strengthening teachings to propose the reported intervention and general mechanism."
